e since 2022, far more than 80%. It is right for a shock month like November 2026 but far too wide in normal times. Proposal: size ranges from recent realized volatility (the adaptive band) instead of a fixed 1.6x."},{"id":"rule5_vix_25pct","belief":"80% VIX bands should be +/-25% of the prior close for one day (rule 5).","verdict":"reject","plain":"A +/-25% one-day VIX band held 99% of days since 2022. Too wide in normal markets; the adaptive band keeps close to 80% and still widens in a storm."},{"id":"adaptive_spx_band","belief":"Size 80% S&P ranges from half VIX + half recent realized vol, width fitted before 2022.","verdict":"adopt","plain":"Fitted on 2016-2021, it held 77% from 2022 on, close to the 80% target. But it held only 53% in the last 15 days, so in a shock it still runs narrow. Proposal: use the wider of the adaptive band and the VIX-implied band once VIX is above 25."},{"id":"lesson_L4_falling_tape","belief":"Don't default to 'up' after a falling week (lesson L4).","verdict":"keep watching","plain":"After a week down 2%+, the next day was up 52% of the time since 2022 (normal 53%). Historically falling weeks did NOT make up days rarer, so L4 as a rule of thumb is not supported by the long record; it may still be right in a specific regime."},{"id":"vix_curve_inverted","belief":"When 3-month VIX is below VIX (inverted curve), the next week moves closer to what VIX prices.","verdict":"adopt","plain":"When the VIX curve inverts, the following week realizes much more of the VIX-implied move than usual, in both halves of history. Proposal: when inverted, do not shrink ranges below the VIX-implied move."},{"id":"setup_analogs_5d","belief":"The setup playbook's 'P(up in 5 days)' from look-alike days beats the plain up-rate.","verdict":"reject","plain":"Tested since 2022 on 245 days using only earlier history: analogs scored 0.245 vs 0.244 for the plain up-rate (lower is better). They do not beat the base rate, so treat the playbook as a picture of the range of outcomes, not as a forecast."},{"id":"specialists_beat_base","belief":"At least one specialist analyst beats the plain up-rate on next-day calls.","verdict":"reject","plain":"Best analyst (rates) scored 0.2481 vs 0.2484 for the plain up-rate across ~1,950 out-of-sample days. A gap that small is noise: none of the simple signals predicts tomorrow's direction."}],"board_record":{"graded":0,"open":10,"band_hit":null,"brier":null,"per_asset":{}},"recent_graded":[]}}],"disclaimer":"Analysis only. Not investment advice."}
